{
 "thread": "XtrmeAiF1CY",
 "subject": "Blind color figures",
 "messages_listed": 3,
 "last_activity": "2025-05-29T11:48:58Z",
 "messages": [
  {
   "id": "4aH6xltnAgAJ",
   "from": "laiaju...@gmail.com",
   "author": "cc62cdc7c1746f0f",
   "date": "2025-05-28T17:08:24Z",
   "subject": "Blind color figures",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "  Hi everyone, I&#39;m about to start the publication process and wanted to ask if anyone might be able to help me with a code that is color-blind friendly but also allows me to keep the same regions in the same color across all figures. <div>Thanks in advance!  </div><div>Laia</div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "SOcq4k2CAgAJ",
   "from": "Jose Luis Mijangos",
   "author": "592079bda2cb3220",
   "date": "2025-05-29T01:22:11Z",
   "subject": "Re: Blind color figures",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<p style=\"margin:0in;font-size:10pt;font-family:Aptos,sans-serif;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\">Hi Laia,</span></p><p style=\"margin:0in;font-size:10pt;font-family:Aptos,sans-serif;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"> </span></p><p style=\"margin:0in;font-size:10pt;font-family:Aptos,sans-serif;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\">Yes, it’s super important to stick with the same colours for each population across all the plots so the reader doesn’t get confused.</span></p><p style=\"margin:0in;font-size:10pt;font-family:Aptos,sans-serif;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"> </span></p><p style=\"margin:0in;font-size:10pt;font-family:Aptos,sans-serif;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\">Here are a few colour-blind friendly options you might find handy:</span></p><p style=\"margin:0in;font-size:10pt;font-family:Aptos,sans-serif;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"> </span></p><p style=\"margin:0in;font-size:10pt;font-family:Aptos,sans-serif;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\">library(dartRverse)</span></p><p style=\"margin:0in;font-size:10pt;font-family:Aptos,sans-serif;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\">t1 &lt;- <a href=\"http://bandicoot.gl\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://bandicoot.gl&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792457501424000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0-rpEw70a6GS-tpJXHuPEC\">bandicoot.gl</a></span></p><p style=\"margin:0in;font-size:10pt;font-family:Aptos,sans-serif;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\">pcoa &lt;- gl.pcoa(t1)</span></p><p style=\"margin:0in;font-size:10pt;font-family:Aptos,sans-serif;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"> </span></p><p style=\"margin:0in;font-size:10pt;font-family:Aptos,sans-serif;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"># Option 1: Adobe Color Wheel (great, but limited to 5 colours)</span></p><p style=\"margin:0in;font-size:10pt;font-family:Aptos,sans-serif;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"># <a href=\"https://color.adobe.com/create/color-accessibility\" title=\"https://color.adobe.com/create/color-accessibility\" style=\"color:rgb(70,120,134);text-decoration-line:underline\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://color.adobe.com/create/color-accessibility&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792457501424000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3M71z9p2VpL6Gth0WBpp-M\">https://color.adobe.com/create/color-accessibility</a></span></p><p style=\"margin:0in;font-size:10pt;font-family:Aptos,sans-serif;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"># Just click the middle of a colour to get the code</span></p><p style=\"margin:0in;font-size:10pt;font-family:Aptos,sans-serif;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\">pop_colors &lt;- c(&quot;#0A09EB&quot;, &quot;#EAE5A6&quot;, &quot;#42CAEA&quot;, &quot;#DAEB09&quot;, &quot;#6B3896&quot;)</span></p><p style=\"margin:0in;font-size:10pt;font-family:Aptos,sans-serif;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\">gl.pcoa.plot(pcoa, x = t1, pt.colors = pop_colors)</span></p><p style=\"margin:0in;font-size:10pt;font-family:Aptos,sans-serif;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"> </span></p><p style=\"margin:0in;font-size:10pt;font-family:Aptos,sans-serif;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"># Option 2: Okabe-Ito palette (one of the best for accessibility!)</span></p><p style=\"margin:0in;font-size:10pt;font-family:Aptos,sans-serif;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"># Info: <a href=\"https://siegal.bio.nyu.edu/color-palette/\" title=\"https://siegal.bio.nyu.edu/color-palette/\" style=\"color:rgb(70,120,134);text-decoration-line:underline\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://siegal.bio.nyu.edu/color-palette/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792457501424000&amp;usg=AOvVaw11x6DroXwG_Srv9F1t8I44\">https://siegal.bio.nyu.edu/color-palette/</a></span></p><p style=\"margin:0in;font-size:10pt;font-family:Aptos,sans-serif;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\">library(pals)</span></p><p style=\"margin:0in;font-size:10pt;font-family:Aptos,sans-serif;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\">pop_colors &lt;- okabe(n = nPop(t1))</span></p><p style=\"margin:0in;font-size:10pt;font-family:Aptos,sans-serif;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\">gl.pcoa.plot(pcoa, x = t1, pt.colors = pop_colors)</span></p><p style=\"margin:0in;font-size:10pt;font-family:Aptos,sans-serif;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"> </span></p><p style=\"margin:0in;font-size:10pt;font-family:Aptos,sans-serif;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"># Option 3: RColorBrewer palettes</span></p><p style=\"margin:0in;font-size:10pt;font-family:Aptos,sans-serif;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\">library(RColorBrewer)</span></p><p style=\"margin:0in;font-size:10pt;font-family:Aptos,sans-serif;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\">display.brewer.all(colorblindFriendly = TRUE)</span></p><p style=\"margin:0in;font-size:10pt;font-family:Aptos,sans-serif;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\">pop_colors &lt;- brewer.pal(n = nPop(t1), name = &quot;Dark2&quot;)</span></p><p style=\"margin:0in;font-size:10pt;font-family:Aptos,sans-serif;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\">gl.pcoa.plot(pcoa, x = t1, pt.colors = pop_colors)</span></p><p style=\"margin:0in;font-size:10pt;font-family:Aptos,sans-serif;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"> </span></p><p style=\"margin:0in;font-size:10pt;font-family:Aptos,sans-serif;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\">Cheers,</span></p><p style=\"margin:0in;font-size:10pt;font-family:Aptos,sans-serif;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\">Luis</span></p>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><div dir=\"auto\" class=\"gmail_attr\">On Thursday, 29 May 2025 at 3:08:24 am UTC+10 <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">laiaju...@gmail.com</a> wrote:<br></div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\">  Hi everyone, I&#39;m about to start the publication process and wanted to ask if anyone might be able to help me with a code that is color-blind friendly but also allows me to keep the same regions in the same color across all figures. <div>Thanks in advance!  </div><div>Laia</div></blockquote></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
